From 76a5d59d0af9ed9765be09ba7a92b2343c2df805 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Beri <jmberi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:16:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] x509: initialise the time passed to x509_crt_find_parent()

x509_crt_verify_chain() passes &now to x509_crt_find_parent(), which only
reads it when MBEDTLS_HAVE_TIME_DATE is defined, and now is only set in
that case. Without MBEDTLS_HAVE_TIME_DATE the value is never read, but
Clang 21 added -Wuninitialized-const-pointer, which reports passing an
uninitialised variable through a const pointer. With
MBEDTLS_FATAL_WARNINGS, the default, that stops the build.

Zero-initialise it, which costs nothing where it is then overwritten.

Found building Zephyr's TLS socket tests with Clang 21, where
MBEDTLS_HAVE_TIME_DATE is off by default.

Assisted-by: Claude:MODEL-VERSION
---
 ChangeLog.d/x509-now-uninitialized.txt | 4 ++++
 library/x509_crt.c                     | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 ChangeLog.d/x509-now-uninitialized.txt

diff --git a/ChangeLog.d/x509-now-uninitialized.txt b/ChangeLog.d/x509-now-uninitialized.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..51bf2c4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ChangeLog.d/x509-now-uninitialized.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+Bugfix
+   * Fix the build with Clang 21 or later and MBEDTLS_FATAL_WARNINGS when
+     MBEDTLS_X509_CRT_PARSE_C is enabled and MBEDTLS_HAVE_TIME_DATE is not.
+     Clang reported -Wuninitialized-const-pointer in x509_crt.c.
diff --git a/library/x509_crt.c b/library/x509_crt.c
index a6fcd1b..c404cf8 100644
--- a/library/x509_crt.c
+++ b/library/x509_crt.c
@@ -2501,7 +2501,7 @@ static int x509_crt_verify_chain(
     int signature_is_good;
     unsigned self_cnt;
     mbedtls_x509_crt *cur_trust_ca = NULL;
-    mbedtls_x509_time now;
+    mbedtls_x509_time now = { 0 };
 
 #if defined(MBEDTLS_HAVE_TIME_DATE)
     if (mbedtls_x509_time_gmtime(mbedtls_time(NULL), &now) != 0) {
-- 
2.43.0

